A :LABEL target followed by Branch() jumps, the legacy goto. The label
statement must not be indented like a block. Branch() matches the stored
label text including the keyword: "LABEL Retry" reaches it, "Retry"
(missing keyword) and "LABEL Missing" (no such label) do not
(diag.branch_target_label); :LABEL itself is deprecated_keyword.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nTry;
nTry := 0;
:LABEL Retry;
nTry += 1;
:IF nTry < 3;
Branch("LABEL Retry");
Branch("Retry");
:ENDIF;
Branch("LABEL Missing");
:RETURN nTry;
-- format --
:DECLARE nTry;
nTry := 0;
:LABEL Retry;
nTry += 1;
:IF nTry < 3;
	Branch("LABEL Retry");
	Branch("Retry");
:ENDIF;
Branch("LABEL Missing");
:RETURN nTry;
